From 3f135289309f0ee6209fc7c2b621875bb6bf8b01 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 16:44:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Preserve literal shell words in printed-pipeline
 compound tracking

Carry quote/escape provenance on ShellWord without changing decoded argv. Only lexical operators and reserved words alter printed-unit or case phases; retain heredoc ownership and inherited stdin flow from PR3210.

Proof: focused regressions 70 fail on base 726ac2e8900d; 93 pass on fix. Full lifecycle: 9830 passed across 54 files. Nine structural/metadata mutants killed; harmless real Bash FED markers prove pipe reachability. Bounded 11-command parser replay changes only three closer repros. Function-indirected producer flow is separately tracked in t_028a39b21383a50d.
---
 cron/lifecycle_guard_nested_shells.py         |  41 +++---
 cron/lifecycle_guard_words.py                 |  16 ++-
 .../test_lifecycle_guard_printed_compounds.py | 133 ++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 171 insertions(+), 19 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 tests/cron/test_lifecycle_guard_printed_compounds.py

diff --git a/cron/lifecycle_guard_nested_shells.py b/cron/lifecycle_guard_nested_shells.py
